w: head. Cry-ing, "A-rise, A-rise, young mar-ried man and come a-long with
"Dm" D6 A,C | D3E DC A,2 | "C" G4 "Dm" A3G | "C" E3D C2 E2 | "Dm" D6 z2 |]
w: me To the low, low lands_ of Hol-land to fight the en-em-y."
%
%leftmargin 1.5in
%
W: 2. Oh I held me love all in my arms still thinking he might stay
W: But the captain he gave another order, he was forced to march away.
W: Crying, "There's many a blithe young married man this night must go with me
W: To the low lowlands of Holland, to fight the enemy".
W:
W: 3. Oh Holland is a wondrous place and in it grows much green
W: Tis a wild inhabitation for me true love to be in
W: Where the grass do grow and the warm winds do blow and there's fruit on every tree
W: But the low lowlands of Holland parted me love and me.
W:
W: 4. No shoe no stocking I'll put on no comb go through my hair
W: Nor shall no coal nor candlelight shine in my bower fair
W: Nor will I lie with any young man until the day I die
W: For the low lowlands of Holland parted me love and I.
%
