L:1/8
Q:1/4=160
K:Dmix
%
A2 A | "D" A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 | A,2D D2E F2G |
w: In the mer-ry month of June, from my home I start-ed,
A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 | "C" E2C C2D EFG |"D" A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 |
w: Left the girls of Tuam near-ly bro-ken heart-ed, Sa-lut-ed fa-ther dear,
A,2D D2E F2G | A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 | "C" E2C C2D EFG |
w:kissed my dar-lin' moth-er, drank a pint of beer, my grief and tears to smother, then
"D" A2d d2B "C" c3 | "D" A2d d2B "C" c3 | "D" A2d d2B "Am" c2A |
w: Off to reap the corn, leave where I was born, cut a stout black-thorn to
"C" G2E C2D EFG |"D" A2d d2B "C" c3 | "D" A2d d2B "C" c3 |
w: ban-ish ghosts and gob-lins, a brand new pair of brogues, ratt-lin' o'er the bogs,
"D" A2d d2B "Am" c2 A/2A/2 | "C" G2E C2D EFG |
w: fright-nin' all the dogs, on the Rock-y Road to Dub _ lin,
[P:Chorus:]"D" A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 | A2D D2E F2G | A2A "C" G2E "D" D3 |
w: One two three four five! Hunt the hare and turn her down the rock-y road,
