w:  Rod-dy Mc-Cor-ley_ goes to die on the bridge of Toome to-day.
%
%%leftmargin 1.5in
%%rightmargin 1.5in
%
W: 2. When last this narrow street he trod, his shining pike in hand,
W: Behind him marched in grim array, a stalwart, earnest band,
W: To Antrim town, To Antrim town, he led them to the fray,
W: But young Roddy McCorley goes to die on the bridge of Toome today.
W:
W: 3. Oh it's up the narrow street he steps, smiling, proud and young,
W: About the hemprope on his neck, the golden ringlets clung,
W: Oh, there's never a tear in his blue eye, so bright and proud are they,
W: And young Roddy McCorley goes to die on the bridge of Toome today.
W:
W: 4. Oh, there's never a one of all your dead more bravely died in fray
W: Than he who marches to his fate on the bridge of Toome today;
W: True to the last! True to the last, he treads the upward way,
W: And young Roddy McCorley goes to die on the bridge of Toome today.
%
